        "prompt": "(i) Differentiate between renewable energy resources and non-renewable energy resources, giving two examples of each.\n(ii) State two environmental advantages of generating electricity using solar photovoltaic panels over crude oil thermal plants.",
        "workedSolution": "(i) Renewable vs. Non-Renewable Energy:\n• **Renewable Energy:** Energy resources that replenish naturally over short timescales and cannot be exhausted by sustainable human consumption (e.g., Solar radiation, Wind energy, Hydroelectric power, Biogas).\n• **Non-Renewable Energy:** Finite terrestrial energy resources that exist in limited amounts and take millions of years to form, becoming depleted once consumed (e.g., Crude petroleum oil, Coal, Natural gas).\n\n(ii) Environmental advantages of solar panels:\n1. **Zero Greenhouse Gas Emissions:** Solar panels produce clean electricity without releasing carbon dioxide (CO₂), sulfur dioxide, or particulate soot during operation.\n2. **Conserves Natural Habitats:** Avoids oil spillage, air pollution, and acid rain associated with drilling, transporting, and burning fossil fuels.",
