        "workedSolution": "(i) Role of *Rhizobium* bacteria:\n*Rhizobium* bacteria live symbiotically in root nodules of leguminous plants. They take unreactive atmospheric nitrogen gas (N₂) and fix it into soluble nitrates and ammonium compounds that the plant uses to synthesize amino acids and proteins. In return, the plant provides the bacteria with carbohydrates and shelter.\n\n(ii) Symptoms of nitrogen deficiency:\n1. **Chlorosis:** Generalized yellowing of foliage, starting on older lower leaves.\n2. **Stunted Growth:** Severely retarded vegetative stem elongation and thin, spindly stalks.",
